Transportation friction represents a major barrier to maintenance behaviour; users often delay or skip maintenance rather than arrange transport to distant service facilities. Collection-based systems remove this friction by bringing service to users. This enables higher maintenance participation rates and earlier intervention when issues emerge.

Reverse logistics systems create economic incentives for manufacturers to design products for efficient transport. Design for safe reverse shipping drives standardization of handling procedures and protective packaging strategies. Feedback from collected condition data enables predictive maintenance modelling and product improvement cycles.